    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Cruise demand remains robust, with strong booking momentum and an upbeat travel environment driving a first-quarter operational beat. The delivery of the new ship *Norwegian Luna* is expanding capacity into a favorable demand backdrop. However, the narrative is tempered by a pullback in the stock from earlier highs and a notable sensitivity to fuel costs; a sharp decline in oil prices provided a relief rally, underscoring how energy volatility continues to weigh on sentiment. Broader cruise sector peers are moving in sympathy, suggesting the dynamics are partly macro-driven.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management exceeded near-term profit expectations but then lowered full-year guidance, creating a mixed signal on forward visibility. The emergence of activist investor Elliott Management as a stakeholder adds a new layer: the market views the pact as a potential catalyst for improved capital discipline or strategic changes, especially given the stock’s prolonged underperformance. Execution will now be judged against both operational delivery and responsiveness to activist pressure, with the integration of new tonnage and cost control as immediate tests of management’s credibility.",
